Subject: [PATCH] sycl: oneDNN weight-only-quantized GEMM for Q8_0 prompt batches (opt-in)

Q8_0 prompt batches wider than the fused XMX dequant GEMM takes (64 tokens) dequantize the whole weight to f16,
then run oneDNN's f16 matmul: a 4096 x 4096 weight writes and rereads 32 MB per batch. GGML_SYCL_WOQ_Q8_0
hands oneDNN the int8 weights instead, as stored in the reorder layout, with the block scales as grouped weight
scales (32 x 1 groups, f16 fpmath applied to the integer weights), so oneDNN widens and scales them inside the
GEMM. The only per-call staging is the scale transpose, [rows][k / 32] -> [k / 32][rows]: 2 bytes per 32 weights.

Ported from kainlan/llama.cpp-intel-optimizations (DnnlGemmWrapper::woq_gemm_q8_0, its V4 probe descriptors),
without its primitive cache, layout tiers and scratch allocator: the descriptors are built per call as in
DnnlGemmWrapper::gemm, oneDNN caching the primitive. The fork measured Mistral 7B Q8_0 pp512 2304 -> 4866 t/s
on an Arc Pro B70 and 1125 -> 2006 on a B50, against its own MMQ, not against this path.

  0  off (default)
  1  the batches the fused XMX GEMM declines (wider than 64 tokens)
  2  every Q8_0 batch that reaches ggml_sycl_op_mul_mat_sycl (more than 8 tokens), ahead of the fused GEMM

The layout exists once a weight has been reordered, which upstream does on its first call of at most 8 tokens.
With the switch on, a prompt batch installs it too (every Q8_0 reader already handles it), so a prompt-only run
reaches the path. It declines into the existing paths, and turns itself off for the run after the first decline:
oneDNN rejects the descriptor, offers only a reference implementation, or throws. The first call logs the
implementation oneDNN picked.

Checked: tools/woq-q8_0-probe runs these descriptors against a double-precision reference (the CPU engine,
with f32 activations since the f16 ones need AVX512-FP16, matches to NMSE 1.6e-13); the backend builds with icpx
2026.2. Not checked: whether Xe-HPG has a non-reference kernel for it, its f16 accuracy, and its speed; the
probe answers all three on the card in a minute.

