 | GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_DNN | 0 or 1 (default)| Enable running computations through oneDNN and always use oneMKL. |
 | GGML_SYCL_FA_ONEDNN | 1 (default) or 0 | Enable the oneDNN fused SDPA (flash-attention) path on supported GPUs. Set to 0 to always use the native SYCL flash-attention kernel. |
 | GGML_SYCL_FA_ONEDNN_DG2_HD64 | 0 (default on Linux) or 1 (default on Windows) | Lets Arc A-series (Alchemist) GPUs run head_dim 64 attention, as in Llama-3.2-1B and Qwen2.5-0.5B, through the oneDNN fused SDPA path. Linux drivers whose IGC predates 2.40 (for example Level Zero 1.15.38646 on Ubuntu 24.04) compute that shape wrongly, so first check `GGML_SYCL_FA_ONEDNN_DG2_HD64=1 test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT -p hsk=64` and set 1 only if it passes. Other head sizes and GPUs are unaffected. |
+| GGML_SYCL_WOQ_Q8_0 | 0 (default), 1 or 2 | Q8_0 prompt batches through oneDNN's weight-only-quantized matmul, which reads the int8 weights in the reorder layout and applies their scales inside the GEMM instead of first writing an f16 copy. 1 takes the batches wider than the fused XMX dequant GEMM handles (64 tokens), 2 every Q8_0 batch of more than 8 tokens. It installs the weight reorder on the first prompt batch, stays off for the run after oneDNN declines once (logged), and needs `GGML_SYCL_DNN=ON` and `GGML_SYCL_F16=ON`. |
 | GGML_SYCL_FA_ONEDNN_MAX_KV | 0 (default, disabled) or positive integer | By default (0), all sequences are handled by the oneDNN fused SDPA path, regardless of KV length; a positive value caps that length, past which sequences fall back to the native kernel. If GPU driver watchdog resets (DEVICE_LOST) occur during long-context inference, set this near the context depth where they start, e.g. 24576. |
 | GGML_SYCL_FA_DPAS | 1 (default) or 0 | Enable the XMX flash-attention kernel for a q4_0 or q8_0 KV cache (`-ctk q4_0 -ctv q4_0` or `-ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0`) on Xe2 or newer GPUs (Arc B-series, Lunar Lake, Panther Lake, Wildcat Lake). It reads the quantized cache directly for decode and batches of up to 31 tokens, head sizes 64, 96, 128, 256 and 512, up to 32 query heads per KV head. Set to 0 to use the native SYCL flash-attention kernels. |
 | GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_VMM | 0 or 1 (default) | Enable the virtual-memory device pool. |
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/gemm.hpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/gemm.hpp
index 81bc5c2e..24eb2174 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/gemm.hpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/gemm.hpp
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@
 #include "dnnl.hpp"
 #include "dnnl_sycl.hpp"
 
+#include <cstring>
+
 class DnnlGemmWrapper {
 public:
     using dt = dnnl::memory::data_type;
@@ -88,6 +90,59 @@ public:
 
         gemm(ctx, m, n, k, a, at, 1, k, k * m, b, bt, 1, k, n * k, c, ct, q, 1, 1);
     }
+
+    // Weight-only-quantized GEMM on the Q8_0 reorder layout: c[n][m] (row stride ldc) = b[n][k] x a[m][k]^T,
+    // with a the int8 qs plane read as stored and a_scales the [k / 32][m] f16 transpose of its d plane. oneDNN
+    // widens the int8 weights to f16 and applies the group scales inside the GEMM (f16 fpmath applied to integer
+    // weights), so the f16 copy of the weights that row_gemm needs is never written. The quantized operand has to
+    // be oneDNN's weights, so the activations are its source here, the other way round from row_gemm.
+    // Returns false, having submitted nothing, when oneDNN rejects the descriptor or only has its reference
+    // implementation, which would be far slower than dequantizing for row_gemm. *impl gets the implementation.
+    static bool woq_q8_0_gemm(ggml_backend_sycl_context & ctx, int m, int n, int k, const int8_t * a,
+                              const sycl::half * a_scales, const sycl::half * b, float * c, int ldc,
+                              const queue_ptr & q, const char ** impl) {
+        constexpr dnnl_dim_t group = 32;  // QK8_0
+        if (k % group != 0) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        auto stream = ctx.stream_dnnl(q);
+        auto eng    = ctx.engine_dnnl(q);
+
+        const auto src_md = dnnl::memory::desc({ n, k }, dt::f16, { k, 1 });
+        const auto wei_md = dnnl::memory::desc({ k, m }, dt::s8, { 1, k });
+        const auto dst_md = dnnl::memory::desc({ n, m }, dt::f32, { ldc, 1 });
+        const auto scl_md = dnnl::memory::desc({ k / group, m }, dt::f16, { m, 1 });
+
+        dnnl::primitive_attr attr;
+        attr.set_scratchpad_mode(dnnl::scratchpad_mode::user);
+        attr.set_scales(DNNL_ARG_WEIGHTS, (1 << 0) | (1 << 1), { group, 1 }, dt::f16);
+        attr.set_fpmath_mode(dnnl::fpmath_mode::f16, /*apply_to_int=*/true);
+
+        dnnl::matmul::primitive_desc pd;
+        try {
+            pd = dnnl::matmul::primitive_desc(eng, src_md, wei_md, dst_md, attr);
+        } catch (const dnnl::error &) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        *impl = pd.impl_info_str();
+        if (std::strncmp(*impl, "ref", 3) == 0) {
+            return false;
+        }
+
+        const auto scratchpad_md = pd.scratchpad_desc();
+        ggml_sycl_pool_alloc<uint8_t> scratchpad(ctx.pool());
+        void * scratchpad_ptr = scratchpad_md.get_size() > 0 ? scratchpad.alloc(scratchpad_md.get_size()) : nullptr;
+
+        std::unordered_map<int, dnnl::memory> args;
+        args.insert({ DNNL_ARG_SRC, dnnl::memory(src_md, eng, const_cast<sycl::half *>(b)) });
+        args.insert({ DNNL_ARG_WEIGHTS, dnnl::memory(wei_md, eng, const_cast<int8_t *>(a)) });
+        args.insert({ DNNL_ARG_DST, dnnl::memory(dst_md, eng, c) });
+        args.insert({ DNNL_ARG_ATTR_SCALES | DNNL_ARG_WEIGHTS, dnnl::memory(scl_md, eng, const_cast<sycl::half *>(a_scales)) });
+        args.insert({ DNNL_ARG_SCRATCHPAD, dnnl::memory(scratchpad_md, eng, scratchpad_ptr) });
+
+        dnnl::matmul(pd).execute(stream, args);
+        return true;
+    }
 };
 
 #endif
